// A `bool` handed to a `*u16` parameter. The port used to auto-ref anything into
// any pointer slot and stamp the node with the SLOT's type, so the argument check
// that ran next compared the slot's type with itself and agreed - the error became
// a silent `&b` and only the C compiler noticed.
fn takes(p: *u16) -> int { return 0; }
fn main() { let b: bool = true; println(takes(b)); }
